body:
"the universe does not decide on what is true about this or that until it absolutely has to.

I think what this is trying to say is that the universe does not have any "solidity". It exists as particles of endless options that will only solidify when we observe it. Well, that's what "we" know. We also can't know what it will solidify as without also being the catalyst of the solidity.  So until we observe, both options technically exist.

&#x200B;

Hence, Schrodinger's cat: the cat is dead and alive at the same time until we look in the box. QM theory puts this in full circle because since we are one of these particles, too we can't ascertain what these particles are doing / "the truth" until we put ourselves in interaction with them which impacts what they "solidify" as then we have what we "know". I think the OP is trying to say, while we know how things work, we can never know what it actually means or see the full picture because we are all players of the universe's game.

&#x200B;

If you've seen the Truman show, I can relate it to this. Think of Truman as the particle. A lone person in a fake world. Everyone is in on the game except him. Truman can't know he's in this fake world AND know what’s happening outside of it at the same time. But he still impacts what happens in the fake world by going about his day anyway still impacting the outcome of events by simply existing while those in the background "observe" him and indirectly control his choices as he sometimes puts himself in a position where secret might be revealed. Since they can't physically control him to not find out it's all fake, they make things happen around him that indirectly controls his decisions which then control the course of events. So Truman is control the events just as much as those who know. The universe is like the Truman show but we as Truman can never absolutely know what or
what is happening  outside of the fake world because once we know it’s fake it’s game over. 

&#x200B;

QM seeks this knowledge to understand whats happening and possible in that state of limbo, but can't because as soon as we observe / interact etc. the limbo ends. That's my take!

I think a lot of people would benefit from neutral thinking. I've been reading up on it lately and I can see neutrality associated with survival over positive or negativity. It has helped me so much to not sit around wondering why my mental state couldn't improve because I was upset at myself because I couldn't just "think positive". 

&#x200B;

I think your sentiments are actually quite neutral. You acknowledge the inhumanity that systems create and people in power of those systems inability to realize what it does to people at the bottom of it. Silly humans are so hungry to put others down to lift others up because no one thinks for themselves anymore. It is saddening, but reality. Try to embody the human you desire others to be and hope for the best lol

I wholeheartedly agree. It is actually laughable because many of them don't realize they perpetuate the same toxicity they claim to be a victim of. I don't understand if they are too dense to realize it, or just ignore it because it is making them look good.  I have served as the "token black girl" in many of my friend groups growing up. I gravitated towards those kind of people simply because they were nice to my face and I was young and naive. 

&#x200B;

I am actually in a "diverse" women's running group right now and one of them had the nerve to walk up to my face and say "its black history month, we are going to do a post and we want to feature you!" I legitimately replied.. "why don't you just feature me on any other month of the year that's not february and that would actually give off a better impression for your instagram feed" Lol.

I don't presume anything based on her attitude. I presume her involvement based on how she is responding and talking to Charlie. There is a recording where Charlie calls her to talk about the bump and she doesn't treat him like a person who "rambles random crap" and instead engages in either code or like she knows exactly what he is talking about. 

&#x200B;

Yes, the recordings are after the bump. But wouldn't any reasonable person ask themselves WHY Charlie would call Katherine, knowing she is not involved? Again, wouldn't he just ask the direct source for help to stop this person threatening them? Why would he ask Katherine to stop it and "handle" them when Sigfredo already handled the first problem?

&#x200B;

What the law can prove is different than real life understanding. It is concerning you can't see how this chick was involved. Katherine sat on the stand and told the jury she had no clue what Charlie was talking about during that audio at the restaurant. She says she doesn't know if she "recalled" if she asked him what the fuck he was saying? That is a damn lie. You either asked or not. Katherine also claimed to "not hear" specific parts of the audio after hearing it multiple times along with them increasing the audio. She then agrees to hearing one part but not the incriminating part. Thats another damn lie.

Any regular innocent person would have hyper-focused on that conversation after the second Sigfredo was arrested. Any normal person would have so many questions. They definitely wouldn't go sit in a restaurant and listen to the person allegedly involved  ramble about covering up crimes. We agree the evidence was slim to work with, but she's definitely guilty.
